hadiths[41]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20814","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, and Muhammad ibn Ja'far, Shu'bah narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Uqbah ibn Suhban, from Ibn Mughaffal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade khadhf and said: It neither defeats an enemy nor hunts game, but it breaks the tooth and puts out the eye."
"20815","Waki' narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan ibn al-Ala, from al-Hasan, from Ibn Mughaffal, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer comes and you are in sheep pens, then pray, and when it comes and you are in camel resting places, then do not pray, for they were created from devils."
"20816","Waki' narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Mughaffal say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited Surah al-Fath in the year of the conquest while on his mount during his journey, and he said once: Surah al-Fath was revealed while he was on a journey, so he began reciting while on his mount, he said: And he repeated melodiously in it. Mu'awiyah said: Were it not that I dislike people gathering around me, I would have demonstrated his recitation to you."
"20817","Shababah and Abu Talib ibn Jaban al-Qari narrated to us, both said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of this hadith. Ibn Jaban said in his hadith: Ah ah."
"20818","Waki' and Ibn Ja'far narrated to us, both said: Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Ibn Buraydah, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Between every two calls to prayer there is a prayer, three times, for whoever wishes."
"20819","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Ghiyath, Abu Na'amah narrated to me, from Ibn Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, he said: Our father, when he heard one of us say: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, would say: Oho, oho; I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr and Umar, and I did not hear any of them say: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate."
"20820","Waki' narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far al-Razi, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Abu al-Aliyah, or from another than him, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, and he was one of the group about whom this verse was revealed: Nor upon those who, when they came to you for you to carry them, to the end of the verse, he said: I was holding a branch of a tree, shading the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with it while they were pledging allegiance to him, and they said: We pledge allegiance to you unto death, he said: No, but do not flee."
"20821","Waki' narrated to us, Abu Sufyan narrated to us, and Ibn Ja'far, Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that dogs are a nation among nations, I would have commanded their killing, so kill from among them every jet-black one."
"20822","Waki' narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan ibn al-Ala, he said: I heard al-Hasan narrating that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that dogs are a nation among nations, I would have commanded their killing, so kill from among them every jet-black one. He said: So a man said to him: O Abu Sa'id, from whom did you hear this? He said: Abdullah ibn Mughaffal narrated it to me, and swore, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), since such-and-such, and he narrated to us in that gathering."
"20823","Sa'd ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn Abi Raitah al-Hadhdha al-Tamimi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad, or Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal al-Muzani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Allah regarding my Companions; Allah, Allah regarding my Companions; do not take them as targets after me; whoever loves them, by my love he loves them, and whoever hates them, by my hatred he hates them; and whoever harms them has harmed me, and whoever harms me has harmed Allah, blessed and exalted, and whoever harms Allah, it is imminent that He will seize him."
"20824","Abdullah ibn Awn al-Kharraz narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Ubaydah ibn Abi Raitah, with the like of this hadith."
"20825","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, that a relative of Abdullah ibn Mughaffal did khadhf, so he forbade him and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade khadhf and said: It neither hunts game nor defeats an enemy, but it breaks the tooth and puts out the eye. He said: So he repeated it, and he said: I narrated to you that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it, then you return to it; I will never speak to you."
"20826","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, and Hasan and Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Buraydah narrated to us, from Abdullah al-Muzani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray two rak'ahs before Maghrib, then he said: Pray two rak'ahs before Maghrib, then he said at the third time: For whoever wishes, out of dislike that people take it as a sunnah."
"20827","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Husayn narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, Abdullah al-Muzani narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not the Bedouins overcome you regarding the name of the Maghrib prayer. He said: And the Bedouins say: It is the Isha."
"20828","Abd al-Samad and Affan narrated to us, both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, and Affan said in his hadith: al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu Na'amah, that Abdullah ibn Mughaffal heard his son say: O Allah, I ask You for the white palace on the right of Paradise when I enter it, so he said: O my son, ask Allah, blessed and exalted, for Paradise and seek refuge in Him from the Fire, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be a people who transgress in supplication and purification."
"20829","Affan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, he said: We were besieging the fortress of Khaybar, and a man threw to us a bag containing fat, so I went to take it, then I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I felt shy."
"20830","Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf narrated to us, he said: Sa'id was asked about prayer in camel resting places, so he informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Basri, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When, meaning you reach the prayer while you are in camel resting places, then do not pray, and when it reaches you in sheep pens, then pray if you wish."
"20831","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Ubaydullah ibn Talhah ibn Ubaydullah ibn Kurayz al-Khuza'i narrated to me, from al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Basri, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal al-Muzani, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not pray in camel resting places, for they were created from the jinn; do you not see their eyes and their restlessness when they shy away? And pray in sheep resting places, for they are closer to mercy."
"20832","Affan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abu Iyas informed us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Mughaffal say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Makkah, while on his she-camel, recited Surah al-Fath. He said: So Abu Iyas recited, then repeated melodiously, and said: Were it not that people would gather around me, I would have recited in this melody."
"20833","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Abu Mas'ud al-Jurayri, Sa'id ibn Iyas, from Qays ibn Abayah, Ibn Abdullah ibn Mughaffal narrated to me, he said: My father said, while I was reciting: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, then when he finished he said: O my son, beware of innovation in Islam, for I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and behind Abu Bakr, and behind Umar and Uthman, may Allah the exalted be pleased with them, and they would not begin the recitation with: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, and I never saw a man to whom innovation was more hateful than him."
"20834","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Kahmas narrated to us, Ibn Buraydah narrated to me, he said: Ibn Mughaffal said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Between every two calls to prayer there is a prayer, between every two calls to prayer there is a prayer, for whoever wishes."
"20835","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Kahmas narrated to us, Ibn Buraydah narrated to me, from Ibn Mughaffal, he said: He saw a man among his companions doing khadhf, so he said: Do not do khadhf, for the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to dislike khadhf, or he said: Forbade it, Kahmas says that, for with it no enemy is defeated and no game is hunted, but it puts out the eye and breaks the tooth. Then he saw him after that doing khadhf, so he said: I inform you that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid khadhf, or dislike it, then I see you doing khadhf; I will not speak to you such-and-such words."
"20836","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that dogs are a nation among nations, I would have commanded their killing, but kill from among them every jet-black one."
"20837","Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, Ash'ath ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to urinate in his washing place, for most whisperings come from it."
"20838","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, he said: I asked al-Hasan about a man keeping a dog in his house, he said: Abdullah ibn Mughaffal narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog, a qirat decreases from his reward every day."
"20839","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Bahz narrated to us, both said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah, Bahz said in his hadith: Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah narrated to me, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Mughaffal al-Muzani say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Makkah on his she-camel reciting Surah al-Fath. He said: So Ibn Mughaffal recited and repeated melodiously, and Mu'awiyah said: Were it not for the people, I would have adopted for you that which Ibn Mughaffal mentioned from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Bahz said in his hadith: Or he carried him on his she-camel. He said: So he recited Surah al-Fath and repeated melodiously in it. Abu Iyas said: Were it not that I fear people would gather around me, I would have repeated melodiously as he repeated."
"20840","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Bahz narrated to us, both said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Mutarrif narrating from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the killing of dogs, then said: What is it with you and dogs? Then he permitted hunting dogs and sheep dogs."
"20841","And he said regarding a vessel when a dog laps in it: Wash it seven times and rub it with dust on the eighth."
"20842","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, he said: A bag of fat was lowered to us on the day of Khaybar, so I jumped and took it, then I looked, and behold the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I felt shy before him."
"20843","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog that is not a hunting dog, or a sheep dog, or a farm dog, then a qirat is decreased from his deeds every day."
"20844","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, Ash'ath informed me, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you urinate in his washing place then perform ablution in it, for most whisperings come from it."
"20845","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: I was with Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, and a man among his people did khadhf near him, then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Isma'il ibn Ulayyah, from Ayyub, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, that a relative of Abdullah ibn Mughaffal did khadhf, so he forbade him."
"20846","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that dogs are a nation among nations, I would have commanded their killing, so kill the jet-black one, and whichever people keep a dog that is not a hunting dog, or for crops, or livestock, a qirat decreases from their rewards every day."
"20847","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray in sheep pens and do not pray in camel resting places, for they were created from devils."
"20848","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The woman, the donkey, and the dog cut off the prayer."
"20849","Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id informed us, from Qatadah, from Uqbah ibn Suhban, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade khadhf and said: With it no game is hunted and no enemy is defeated, but it puts out the eye and breaks the tooth. And Yazid said once: With it no game is hunted and no enemy is defeated."
"20850","Yazid narrated to us, al-Jurayri and Kahmas informed us, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: At every two calls to prayer there is a prayer, at every two calls to prayer there is a prayer, at every two calls to prayer there is a prayer, for whoever wishes."
"20851","Rawh narrated to us, Ash'ath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays over a funeral, he has a qirat, and if he waits until it is finished, he has two qirats."
"20852","Sa'id ibn Amir narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog that is not a hunting dog, nor for crops, nor sheep, then a qirat decreases from his reward every day."
"20853","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Thabit Abu Zayd narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Zayd al-Raqashi narrated to me, he said, Abd al-Samad said in his hadith: From Fudayl ibn Zayd, and he had campaigned with Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, in seven campaigns, he said: I asked Abdullah ibn Mughaffal al-Muzani: What drink has been forbidden to us? He said: Khamr. He said: So I said: This is in the Quran. So he said: I will not inform you except what I heard Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or the Messenger of Allah, Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say, either he began with the message or began with the name, so I said: My condition is that I have sufficed, he said: So he said: He forbade the hantam, and it is the jar, and he forbade the dubba, and it is the gourd, and he forbade the muzaffat, and it is what is smeared with tar, of a skin or other than it, and he forbade the naqir. He said: When I heard that, I bought a waterskin, and here it is, hanging, in which nabidh is made."
"20854","Sa'id ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn Abi Raitah al-Hadhdha al-Tamimi narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad, or Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal al-Muzani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Allah regarding my Companions; Allah, Allah regarding my Companions; do not take them as targets after me; whoever loves them, by my love he loves them, and whoever hates them, by my hatred he hates them; and whoever harms them has harmed me, and whoever harms me has harmed Allah, mighty and majestic, and whoever harms Allah, it is imminent that He will seize him."
